BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain First-Class Functions and Higher-Order Functions in Python. Implement custom versions of map\(\), filter\(\), and reduce\(\) with lambda expressions.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. First-Class Functions Principle:) Tj
T*
(   In Python, functions are first-class objects, meaning they can be:) Tj
T*
(   1. Assigned to variables and data structure slots.) Tj
T*
(   2. Passed as arguments into other functions.) Tj
T*
(   3. Returned as return values from functions.) Tj
T*
(   4. Dynamically created at runtime.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Higher-Order Functions:) Tj
T*
(   A higher-order function is any function that takes one or more functions as parameters or) Tj
T*
(   returns a function.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Custom Implementations of map\(\), filter\(\), and reduce\(\):) Tj
T*
(   - custom_map\(func, iterable\): Applies transformation func to each item.) Tj
T*
(   - custom_filter\(predicate, iterable\): Retains items where predicate\(item\) is True.) Tj
T*
(   - custom_reduce\(func, iterable, initializer=None\): Iteratively aggregates elements using a) Tj
T*
(   binary operator.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def my_map\(func, iterable\):) Tj
T*
(   """Custom generator implementation of map\(\).""") Tj
T*
(   for item in iterable:) Tj
T*
(   yield func\(item\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def my_filter\(predicate, iterable\):) Tj
T*
(   """Custom generator implementation of filter\(\).""") Tj
T*
(   for item in iterable:) Tj
T*
(   if predicate\(item\):) Tj
T*
(   yield item) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def my_reduce\(func, iterable, initializer=None\):) Tj
T*
(   """Custom accumulator implementation of reduce\(\).""") Tj
T*
(   it = iter\(iterable\)) Tj
T*
(   if initializer is None:) Tj
T*
(   try:) Tj
T*
(   accumulator = next\(it\)) Tj
T*
(   except StopIteration:) Tj
T*
(   raise TypeError\("reduce\(\) of empty iterable with no initial value"\)) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   accumulator = initializer) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for item in it:) Tj
T*
(   accumulator = func\(accumulator, item\)) Tj
T*
(   return accumulator) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   nums = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Square numbers via my_map) Tj
T*
(   squared = list\(my_map\(lambda x: x ** 2, nums\)\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"my_map \(x^2\): {squared}"\)) Tj
T*
ET

