(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Mathematical Functions in Python's standard math module. Detail trigonometry, logarithms, power, ceiling/floor, and special constants \(pi, e, inf, nan\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Architecture of Python's math Module:) Tj
T*
(   The math module provides direct, high-performance wrappers around the underlying platform C) Tj
T*
(   library \(libm\) mathematical routines. All functions operate on and return standard IEEE 754) Tj
T*
(   64-bit floating-point numbers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Core Functional Groupings:) Tj
T*
(   1. Trigonometry & Angular Conversions:) Tj
T*
(   - math.sin\(x\), math.cos\(x\), math.tan\(x\): Angle x strictly in radians.) Tj
T*
(   - math.radians\(deg\): deg * \(pi / 180\).) Tj
T*
(   - math.degrees\(rad\): rad * \(180 / pi\).) Tj
T*
(   - math.atan2\(y, x\): Arc tangent returning angle in correct quadrant [-pi, pi].) Tj
T*
(   2. Power & Logarithms:) Tj
T*
(   - math.sqrt\(x\), math.isqrt\(n\) \(Exact integer square root\).) Tj
T*
(   - math.exp\(x\) \(e^x\), math.log\(x[, base]\) \(Natural log by default, or arbitrary base\).) Tj
T*
(   - math.log10\(x\), math.log2\(x\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Rounding & Truncation:) Tj
T*
(   - math.ceil\(x\): Smallest integer >= x.) Tj
T*
(   - math.floor\(x\): Greatest integer <= x.) Tj
T*
(   - math.trunc\(x\): Truncates towards zero.) Tj
T*
(   4. Constants:) Tj
T*
(   - math.pi \(3.141592653589793\), math.e \(2.718281828459045\), math.inf \(Infinity\), math.nan) Tj
T*
(   \(Not-a-Number\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import math) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def scientific_calculator_demo\(\):) Tj
T*
(   angle_deg = 45.0) Tj
T*
(   rad = math.radians\(angle_deg\)) Tj
T*
