(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Recursion Limit in Python. Detail RecursionError, sys.getrecursionlimit\(\), sys.setrecursionlimit\(\), and why Python avoids Tail Call Optimization \(TCO\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Python's Recursion Limit and Stack Safety:) Tj
T*
(   Unlike languages with unbounded stacks or automatic TCO, CPython runs on top of the host) Tj
T*
(   operating system's C execution stack.) Tj
T*
(   Each Python stack frame corresponds to an underlying C call to PyEval_EvalFrameDefault. If) Tj
T*
(   unchecked, infinite recursion would exhaust OS stack memory, triggering an uncatchable) Tj
T*
(   Segmentation Fault and crashing the entire process!) Tj
T*
(   To safeguard against this, CPython maintains a hard recursion counter. When stack depth reaches) Tj
T*
(   sys.getrecursionlimit\(\) \(typically 1000\), Python throws a catchable RecursionError \(a subclass) Tj
T*
(   of RuntimeError\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Inspecting and Adjusting Recursion Limit:) Tj
T*
(   - sys.getrecursionlimit\(\): Returns current limit.) Tj
T*
(   - sys.setrecursionlimit\(limit\): Increases or decreases limit.) Tj
T*
(   Caution: Setting the limit excessively high \(e.g. 500,000\) risks crashing the interpreter if) Tj
T*
(   physical OS stack memory overflows.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Why Python Deliberately Omits Tail Call Optimization \(TCO\):) Tj
T*
(   Tail Call Optimization \(TCO\) allows a compiler to overwrite the current stack frame with the) Tj
T*
(   child frame if the recursive call is in tail position, reducing stack space from O\(N\) to O\(1\).) Tj
T*
(   Guido van Rossum explicitly rejected TCO in Python because:) Tj
T*
(   1. Stack Trace Preservation: TCO destroys intermediary stack frames. In production, when an) Tj
T*
(   exception occurs, debugging relies on having the complete, accurate stack trace showing every) Tj
T*
(   line of code executed.) Tj
T*
(   2. Language Philosophy: Python encourages clean iteration \(for / while\) over deep recursion.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Default CPython Recursion Limit: {sys.getrecursionlimit\(\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def test_recursion_depth\(n\):) Tj
T*
ET

