/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement Binary Search recursively in Python. Detail subproblem partitioning, mid calculation, base cases, and compare with iterative implementation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Formulation of Recursive Binary Search:) Tj
T*
(   Binary Search operates on a sorted collection by recursively partitioning the search space in) Tj
T*
(   half:) Tj
T*
(   1. Base Cases:) Tj
T*
(   - Success: arr[mid] == target -> Return mid.) Tj
T*
(   - Failure: low > high -> Return -1 \(Target does not exist in array\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Recursive Steps:) Tj
T*
(   - If arr[mid] < target: Recurse on right subarray: search\(mid + 1, high\).) Tj
T*
(   - If arr[mid] > target: Recurse on left subarray: search\(low, mid - 1\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Midpoint Calculation:) Tj
T*
(   mid = low + \(high - low\) // 2 prevents integer overflow in fixed-width arithmetic languages and) Tj
T*
(   ensures proper integer truncation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def binary_search_recursive\(arr: list, target: int, low=0, high=None\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   if high is None:) Tj
T*
(   high = len\(arr\) - 1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Base Case: Search boundary exhausted) Tj
T*
(   if low > high:) Tj
T*
(   return -1) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   mid = low + \(high - low\) // 2) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Base Case: Target found) Tj
T*
(   if arr[mid] == target:) Tj
T*
(   return mid) Tj
T*
(   # Recursive Step 1: Search right half) Tj
T*
(   elif arr[mid] < target:) Tj
T*
(   return binary_search_recursive\(arr, target, mid + 1, high\)) Tj
T*
(   # Recursive Step 2: Search left half) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   return binary_search_recursive\(arr, target, low, mid - 1\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   sorted_data = [5, 12, 19, 27, 34, 45, 56, 68, 79, 91]) Tj
T*
(   target1 = 45) Tj
T*
ET

