(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Memoization and Dynamic Programming. Implement the Fibonacci sequence and compare naive recursive O\(2^N\), manual memoization O\(N\), and @lru_cache.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Problem of Redundant Subproblems:) Tj
T*
(   The naive recursive Fibonacci algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   def fib\(n\): return fib\(n-1\) + fib\(n-2\)) Tj
T*
(   exhibits severe overlapping subproblems. Computing fib\(5\) computes fib\(3\) twice, fib\(2\) three) Tj
T*
(   times, and fib\(1\) five times!) Tj
T*
(   Total calls branch exponentially: O\(2^N\). Computing fib\(40\) requires over 2 billion recursive) Tj
T*
(   calls!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Memoization \(Top-Down Dynamic Programming\):) Tj
T*
(   Memoization is an optimization technique that caches the return values of expensive pure) Tj
T*
(   function calls keyed on input arguments. When called with the same arguments again, the) Tj
T*
(   function returns the cached result in O\(1\) time.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import time) Tj
T*
(   from functools import lru_cache) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 1. Manual Memoization using Dictionary Cache) Tj
T*
(   def fib_manual_memo\(n: int, memo=None\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   if memo is None:) Tj
T*
(   memo = {0: 0, 1: 1}) Tj
T*
(   if n not in memo:) Tj
T*
(   memo[n] = fib_manual_memo\(n - 1, memo\) + fib_manual_memo\(n - 2, memo\)) Tj
T*
(   return memo[n]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # 2. Automated Memoization using @lru_cache) Tj
T*
(   @lru_cache\(maxsize=None\)) Tj
T*
(   def fib_lru_cached\(n: int\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   if n <= 1:) Tj
T*
(   return n) Tj
T*
(   return fib_lru_cached\(n - 1\) + fib_lru_cached\(n - 2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Benchmark Comparison) Tj
T*
(   n_target = 35) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Manual Memoization Benchmark) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
