(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Recursive QuickSort algorithm in Python with Hoare/Lomuto partitioning. Compare worst-case O\(N^2\) vs average-case O\(N log N\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis of QuickSort:) Tj
T*
(   QuickSort is an in-place divide-and-conquer sorting algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   1. Choose a Pivot element from the array.) Tj
T*
(   2. Partition the array into three partitions: elements < pivot, elements == pivot, and elements) Tj
T*
(   > pivot.) Tj
T*
(   3. Recursively sort the sub-arrays.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Performance Trade-Off:) Tj
T*
(   - Average Time: O\(N log2 N\) with small constant factors.) Tj
T*
(   - Worst Case: O\(N^2\) if the pivot is consistently chosen as the smallest or largest element on) Tj
T*
(   already sorted data.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(log N\) stack frames with randomized pivot.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def quicksort_idiomatic\(arr: list\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   if len\(arr\) <= 1:) Tj
T*
