(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Recursive Backtracking Maze Solver in Python using 2D grids, finding a path from start \(0,0\) to exit \(M-1, N-1\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Formulation of Maze Solving via Backtracking:) Tj
T*
(   Given an M x N grid where:) Tj
T*
(   0 = Open Path, 1 = Wall / Obstacle.) Tj
T*
(   Objective: Find a path from \(0, 0\) to \(M - 1, N - 1\) moving only Up, Down, Left, Right.) Tj
T*
(   Backtracking Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   1. Base Cases:) Tj
T*
(   - Success: \(r, c\) == \(M - 1, N - 1\) -> Target reached!) Tj
T*
(   - Invalid: \(r, c\) out of bounds, cell is a wall \(1\), or cell already visited \(2\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Mark cell as visited: maze[r][c] = 2.) Tj
T*
(   3. Explore 4 cardinal directions recursively:) Tj
T*
ET

