(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Function Annotations and Type Hints \(PEP 484\) in Python. Contrast dynamic typing with static type checking using mypy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Type Hints and PEP 484 Specification:) Tj
T*
(   Introduced in Python 3.5, Type Annotations provide a standardized syntax for specifying the) Tj
T*
(   expected types of function parameters and return values:) Tj
T*
(   def process\(data: list[int], threshold: float = 0.5\) -> dict[str, bool]:) Tj
T*
(   Key Properties:) Tj
T*
(   - Pure Metadata: Type hints are completely ignored by the Python runtime. Python remains a) Tj
T*
(   dynamically-typed language; passing a float into an int parameter does NOT raise an error at) Tj
T*
(   runtime.) Tj
T*
(   - Stored in __annotations__: Annotations are compiled into a dictionary accessible at runtime) Tj
T*
(   via func.__annotations__.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Static Analysis via Mypy:) Tj
T*
(   External static analysis tools like mypy inspect type annotations before execution, catching) Tj
T*
(   bugs, type mismatches, and None dereferencing errors during CI/CD build pipelines without) Tj
T*
(   incurring runtime performance penalties.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   from typing import Union, Optional) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def compute_risk_score\() Tj
T*
(   client_id: str,) Tj
T*
(   annual_income: float,) Tj
T*
(   credit_score: int,) Tj
T*
(   flags: Optional[list[str]] = None) Tj
T*
(   \) -> dict[str, Union[float, str]]:) Tj
T*
(   """Type-annotated enterprise risk scoring function.""") Tj
T*
(   if flags is None:) Tj
T*
(   flags = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   score = \(annual_income / 100_000.0\) * 0.4 + \(credit_score / 850.0\) * 0.6) Tj
T*
(   category = "LOW" if score > 0.7 else "MEDIUM" if score > 0.4 else "HIGH") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   return {) Tj
T*
(   "ClientID": client_id,) Tj
T*
(   "Score": round\(score, 4\),) Tj
T*
(   "Category": category) Tj
T*
(   }) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Inspect annotations at runtime) Tj
T*
(   print\("Function __annotations__ Metadata:"\)) Tj
T*
(   for param, p_type in compute_risk_score.__annotations__.items\(\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f" {param:<15} -> {p_type}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   result = compute_risk_score\("CL-901", 120_000.0, 750\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Computed Result: {result}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Runtime Overhead: O\(1\) dictionary compilation at function creation; zero call overhead.) Tj
T*
ET

