/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Generator Functions and the yield Keyword. Contrast generators with standard return functions in memory usage and streaming pipelines.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundations of Generators \(PEP 255\):) Tj
T*
(   A standard Python function executes from top to bottom, returns a single value via return, and) Tj
T*
(   destroys its stack frame and local variables.) Tj
T*
(   A Generator Function is defined using the standard def syntax, but contains one or more yield) Tj
T*
(   expressions:) Tj
T*
(   - When invoked, it does NOT execute the code; it returns a generator iterator object.) Tj
T*
(   - When next\(gen\) is called, execution advances until a yield expression is reached.) Tj
T*
(   - The yielded value is returned to the caller, and the function's entire execution context) Tj
T*
(   \(instruction pointer, local variables, evaluation stack\) is frozen in place!) Tj
T*
(   - Subsequent calls to next\(gen\) resume execution immediately after the yield statement.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Memory Efficiency: Lazy Evaluation:) Tj
T*
(   Generating 100,000,000 numbers in a list requires gigabytes of RAM. A generator produces values) Tj
T*
(   lazily on-demand in O\(1\) constant memory.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   import sys) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def fibonacci_infinite_stream\(\):) Tj
T*
(   """Infinite generator stream of Fibonacci numbers.""") Tj
T*
(   a, b = 0, 1) Tj
T*
(   while True:) Tj
T*
(   yield a) Tj
T*
(   a, b = b, a + b) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Streaming pipeline) Tj
T*
(   fib_gen = fibonacci_infinite_stream\(\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Memory Size of Generator Object: {sys.getsizeof\(fib_gen\)} bytes \(O\(1\) Memory!\)"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   first_8 = [next\(fib_gen\) for _ in range\(8\)]) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"First 8 Fibonacci Stream Elements: {first_8}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
