(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Recursive Flattening algorithm for arbitrarily nested lists of irregular depths in Python with type checking.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   Given a nested list of heterogeneous elements and irregular nesting depths \(e.g., [1, [2, [3,) Tj
T*
(   [4, 5]], 6], 7]\), flatten it into a single one-dimensional list [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Recursive Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   Traverse each item in the list:) Tj
T*
(   - If item is a list or tuple \(compound collection\): Recursively call flatten\(item\) and extend) Tj
T*
(   the result.) Tj
T*
(   - Else: Append the scalar leaf element directly.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def flatten_nested_list\(nested_data: list\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   flat = []) Tj
T*
(   for item in nested_data:) Tj
T*
(   if isinstance\(item, \(list, tuple\)\):) Tj
T*
(   # Recursive step) Tj
T*
(   flat.extend\(flatten_nested_list\(item\)\)) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   # Base case: scalar element) Tj
T*
(   flat.append\(item\)) Tj
T*
(   return flat) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Alternative: Generator implementation using 'yield from') Tj
T*
(   def flatten_generator\(nested_data\):) Tj
T*
(   for item in nested_data:) Tj
T*
(   if isinstance\(item, \(list, tuple\)\):) Tj
T*
(   yield from flatten_generator\(item\)) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   yield item) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   complex_nested = [1, [2, [3, 4], 5], [[6, 7], 8], 9]) Tj
T*
(   result_flat = flatten_nested_list\(complex_nested\)) Tj
T*
(   gen_flat = list\(flatten_generator\(complex_nested\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Original Nested: {complex_nested}"\)) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
