(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a String Permutation and Combination generator in Python without external libraries using recursive backtracking and list swapping.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Basis:) Tj
T*
(   Generating all permutations of a string of length N requires exploring N! unique arrangements.) Tj
T*
(   Backtracking Algorithm:) Tj
T*
(   Swap each character into the current position, recurse for the remainder of the string, and) Tj
T*
(   swap back to restore original state \(backtrack\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def find_permutations\(text: str\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   chars = list\(text\)) Tj
T*
(   n = len\(chars\)) Tj
T*
(   perms = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def backtrack\(start\):) Tj
T*
(   if start == n:) Tj
T*
(   perms.append\("".join\(chars\)\)) Tj
T*
(   return) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for i in range\(start, n\):) Tj
T*
(   # Swap) Tj
T*
(   chars[start], chars[i] = chars[i], chars[start]) Tj
T*
(   # Recurse) Tj
T*
(   backtrack\(start + 1\)) Tj
T*
(   # Backtrack) Tj
T*
(   chars[start], chars[i] = chars[i], chars[start]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   backtrack\(0\)) Tj
T*
(   return perms) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   sample = "CAT") Tj
T*
(   all_perms = find_permutations\(sample\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"All Permutations of '{sample}' \(Total: {len\(all_perms\)}\): {all_perms}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N * N!\) operations.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(N\) call stack frames.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
