(   1. Problem Context:) Tj
T*
(   Given a string s = 'aab', partition s such that every substring of the partition is a) Tj
T*
(   palindrome. Return all possible palindrome partitioning configurations \(e.g., [['a', 'a', 'b'],) Tj
T*
(   ['aa', 'b']]\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Backtracking Strategy:) Tj
T*
(   1. Base Case: If start index reaches len\(s\), add current partition snapshot to results.) Tj
T*
(   2. For end in range\(start, len\(s\)\):) Tj
T*
(   Extract substring = s[start : end + 1].) Tj
T*
(   If substring is a palindrome \(substring == substring[::-1]\):) Tj
T*
(   - Append to current partition.) Tj
T*
(   - Recurse for end + 1.) Tj
T*
(   - Pop substring to backtrack.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def partition_palindromes\(s: str\) -> list:) Tj
T*
(   results = []) Tj
T*
(   current_path = []) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def is_palindrome\(sub: str\) -> bool:) Tj
T*
(   return sub == sub[::-1]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def backtrack\(start: int\):) Tj
T*
(   if start == len\(s\):) Tj
T*
(   results.append\(list\(current_path\)\)) Tj
T*
(   return) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   for end in range\(start, len\(s\)\):) Tj
T*
(   substring = s[start : end + 1]) Tj
T*
(   if is_palindrome\(substring\):) Tj
T*
(   current_path.append\(substring\)) Tj
T*
(   backtrack\(end + 1\)) Tj
T*
(   current_path.pop\(\) # Backtrack) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   backtrack\(0\)) Tj
T*
(   return results) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Verification) Tj
T*
(   target = "aab") Tj
T*
(   partitions = partition_palindromes\(target\)) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Palindrome Partitions for '{target}': {partitions}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Time Complexity: O\(N * 2^N\) exponential combinations.) Tj
T*
(   - Space Complexity: O\(N\) recursive call stack.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
