(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Partial Function Application using functools.partial in Python. Contrast partial application with Currying with practical examples.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Partial Application \(functools.partial\):) Tj
T*
(   Partial application fixes a subset of a function's arguments, returning a new callable with a) Tj
T*
(   reduced arity:) Tj
T*
(   partial\(func, *fixed_args, **fixed_kwargs\)) Tj
T*
(   Currying decomposes a multi-argument function f\(a, b, c\) into a chain of single-argument) Tj
T*
(   functions: f\(a\)\(b\)\(c\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Code Demonstration:) Tj
T*
(   from functools import partial) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   def power\(base: float, exponent: float\) -> float:) Tj
T*
(   return base ** exponent) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Partial application: fix exponent=2 \(Square\) and exponent=3 \(Cube\)) Tj
T*
(   square = partial\(power, exponent=2\)) Tj
T*
(   cube = partial\(power, exponent=3\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   print\(f"Square\(8\): {square\(8\)} | Cube\(5\): {cube\(5\)}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   # Practical Enterprise Use Case: Pre-configured API Logger) Tj
T*
(   def log_message\(level: str, service: str, message: str\):) Tj
T*
(   print\(f"[{level:<7}] [{service:<10}] {message}"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   auth_logger = partial\(log_message, "AUTH_SVC"\)) Tj
T*
(   error_logger = partial\(log_message, "CRITICAL", "DATABASE"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   error_logger\("Connection pool exhausted on port 5432!"\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Complexity Analysis:) Tj
T*
(   - Call Overhead: O\(1\) argument merging in C wrapper.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
