12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Implement a Trampoline pattern in Python to eliminate recursion stack overflow for deep tail-recursive algorithms.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Problem of Stack Limits in Tail Recursion:) Tj
T*
(   Because Python does not support Tail Call Optimization, tail-recursive functions still consume) Tj
T*
(   O\(N\) stack frames.) Tj
T*
(   For N = 100,000, recursion limit is exceeded.) Tj
T*
(   A Trampoline is an iterative design pattern that repeatedly calls thunk-returning functions in) Tj
T*
(   a while loop, running unbounded recursion in O\(1\) stack memory!) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   class Trampoline:) Tj
T*
(   @staticmethod) Tj
T*
(   def call\(func, *args, **kwargs\):) Tj
T*
(   res = func\(*args, **kwargs\)) Tj
T*
(   while callable\(res\):) Tj
T*
(   res = res\(\)) Tj
T*
ET

