(   [Problem Statement]: Implement the Ackermann Function in Python with recursion analysis, rapid growth metrics, and recursion limit protection.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Formulation of the Ackermann-Peter Function:) Tj
T*
(   A\(m, n\) is a classic example of a computable function that is not primitive recursive:) Tj
T*
(   - If m == 0: A\(0, n\) = n + 1) Tj
T*
(   - If m > 0 and n == 0: A\(m, 0\) = A\(m - 1, 1\)) Tj
T*
(   - If m > 0 and n > 0: A\(m, n\) = A\(m - 1, A\(m, n - 1\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Python Implementation:) Tj
T*
(   def ackermann\(m: int, n: int\) -> int:) Tj
T*
(   """Compute Ackermann function with call depth logging.""") Tj
T*
(   if m == 0:) Tj
T*
(   return n + 1) Tj
T*
(   elif n == 0:) Tj
T*
(   return ackermann\(m - 1, 1\)) Tj
T*
(   else:) Tj
T*
(   return ackermann\(m - 1, ackermann\(m, n - 1\)\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

